{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1078203-can-changelings-go-back-to-arcadia","id":1078203,"title":"Can Changelings go back to Arcadia?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-14T00:15:12-07:00","id":1078203,"title":"Can Changelings go back to Arcadia?","content":"This might seem like a weird question but bear with me.<br /> <br /> I've only actually played a few sessions of a Changeling game <i>once</i>, so I'm not as familiar as y'all here in the Changeling forum.<br /> <br /> To my VERY LIMITED (!!!) understanding, there are three major &quot;worlds&quot; in Changeling:<br /> <br /> The Mundane World: Our world. No differences.<br /> <br /> The Hedge: A mystical &quot;World Between The Worlds&quot; where people from various &quot;Arcadian Realms&quot; come together to sell produce. (???)<br /> <br /> Arcadia: The world of fantasy, story, and wonder.<br /> <br /> Any Changeling's durance in Arcadia can be whatever they want to be - a hot scalding desert, a frozen tundra, a deep taiga, a beautiful meadowland, a vast ocean - because Arcadia is made of tropes and can have as many levels and made-up continents as you want.<br /> <br /> In the game that I played, Arcadia was purely a backstory thing. It didn't come up again in game. You can go to the Hedge to pick up magical groceries (???) but you're risking a lot by going to that world between the worlds, but going beyond into Arcadia was effectively suicide.<br /> <br /> Is that how it's supposed to go, or do Changelings frequently go to Arcadia to battle Fae and what not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T00:22:59-07:00","id":1078205,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing you're being a little glib in your descriptions, but in case you're not the Hedge isn't just a marketplace, it's also a labyrinth of fear and lost souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1078203-can-changelings-go-back-to-arcadia#post1078203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that how it's supposed to go, or do Changelings frequently go to Arcadia to battle Fae and what not?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say frequently, but it's certainly an option, it comes up in some of the books in first edition. And to many that would be 'effectively suicide.'<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind I don't know how this has changed in second edition, so far its seemed like the Fae were more distant and indomitable, like a piece of background. That's just a feeling though.<br /> <br /> And obviously you could get captured again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-14-2017, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T00:41:07-07:00","id":1078209,"title":"","content":"Arcadia is made up of agreements between concrete and abstract forces and the fae. People who were taken there and became changelings were effectively part of the collection of pacts and bargains that made up their Keeper's greater identity, and getting out required them to assert that they effectively weren't the person that was bound up in that chunk of the web; even without the threat of the Fae (who are not lightly equated with gods in their own domains), going back to Arcadia is bad news for the Lost because it threatens to erode their sense of place as someone partially defined by <i>leaving Arcadia</i>.<br /> <br /> Arcadia is both more and less mutable than the Hedge, in that the whims of the Gentry are more immediately manifest there while still being under a more unified banner of script-direction than the no-man's-land that separates the Jeweled Realm from Earth \u2014 Faerie obeys the Fae as deed follows thought, and this means the most fanciful things the Wyrd knows of can often only survive in an Arcadian bell-jar unless there's some key interest in maintaining it elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The Hedge is the road and the wall between worlds, and in the hollow spaces where the Strangers seldom look Their spurned suitors and runaway pets carve out a living and engage in the fickle economics of buying silence and selling dreams (and weirder things besides).<br /> <br /> Goblin fruits are more than produce and groceries. They're one-use tradeoffs of a kind with the Glamour-infused magic of tokens \u2014 eating a flower grown on heartsblood and solitude might strengthen your resolve at the cost of your voice for the span of dawn to dusk, and a strange tuber pulled from a derelict farm-garden might fill your gut with worms for hours while enabling you to speak with the dead. They're a common enough thing to find vendors selling at a goblin market, but the fae of the Hedge sell more than food and falsehoods \u2014 everything from relics to retainers to abstract phenomena might be sold somewhere among the Thorns, if you could only find the price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T00:42:29-07:00","id":1078210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1078203-can-changelings-go-back-to-arcadia?p=1078205#post1078205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing you're being a little glib in your descriptions, but in case you're not the Hedge isn't just a marketplace, it's also a labyrinth of fear and lost souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was only being a little glib. I knew there had to be more to the Hedge, but I was always told it was just a place where you could buy magic groceries. Labyrinth of Fear and Lost Souls definitely adds to the interest factor.<br /> <br /> And yeah, so, I guess it really just is that - Arcadia is a distant, out-of-scope setting. I just didn't know if some of your average game was supposed to take place there in addition to backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T01:46:00-07:00","id":1078222,"title":"","content":"Your average game isn't going to do scenes in Arcadia, no. You <i>can </i>go back there during play, but it's meant to be like a major big deal, a once-in-a-campaign thing. You're not expected to be going back and forth. The 1st edition sourcebook Equinox Road has rules for actually physically returning to Arcadia and running a story there, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T02:02:52-07:00","id":1078225,"title":"","content":"I massively appreciate your description, Satchel. Flowery descriptions of Changeling locations always get me excited to try it out (once 2e finally hits the shelves...metaphorically.)<br /> <br /> I checked out the description of Equinox Road on DTRPG and it even says there that it's 'end game' material. <br /> <br /> FWIW, I was only wondering because I didn't know if I was right about Arcadia being a place you avoided at all cost and was otherwise End Game, or whether that was a weird house interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T08:05:28-07:00","id":1078359,"title":"","content":"To quote the book:<br /> &quot;Changeling: The Lost stories don\u2019t typically take place in Arcadia. Our stories focus on what the Lost do once they\u2019ve escaped. Returning is functionally a death sentence for most changelings. But there are a few reasons to tell tales within Arcadia. Here are a few ideas about how you might use Arcadia:&quot;<br /> <br /> Possible in a few epic cases, but not something casual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T08:22:31-07:00","id":1078366,"title":"","content":"Physically, going back to Arcadia is completely possible, and not even dreadfully hard. But, as others have said, changelings have good reasons not to <i>want</i> to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}